# Code owners for the QuixLakeHouse Grafana data source plugin.
#
# Every pull request requires approval from one of these owners. Combined with a
# ruleset on `main` that has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled, this is
# what guarantees an outside contributor cannot merge into a public repo.
#
# When a line lists more than one team, approval from ANY ONE of them satisfies
# the requirement -- so co-listing quix-saas is a safety net, not extra friction.
#
# Team access as configured on this repo: customer-success (admin),
# infra-team (admin), quix-saas (push). A team needs at least write/push access
# or GitHub silently ignores its entry here.

# Default owner: Customer Success owns this plugin (Shortcut sc-74412).
*                           @quixio/customer-success

# Go backend -- query path, auth handling, Arrow conversion. Platform
# engineering can also approve, since it touches the lakehouse API contract.
/pkg/                       @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas

# Frontend -- config editor, query editor, datasource wiring.
/src/                       @quixio/customer-success

# Anything that changes how the plugin is built, signed or published.
# A bad change here can publish a broken artifact to the Grafana catalog.
/.github/                   @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas
/Magefile.go                @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas
/package.json               @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas
/src/plugin.json            @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas

# Deployment-shaped files: provisioning and the dev compose stack.
/provisioning/              @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas
/docker-compose.dev.yml     @quixio/customer-success @quixio/quix-saas
